  "body": "## Problem reproduced from runtime logs\n\nThe Observer itself was not failing, but it was far too slow to fill Price Matrix / market statistics:\n- only 6 of 76 models were fully recorded in roughly 9 minutes,\n- the first browser batch of 3 models took about 6 minutes,\n- every newly discovered listing triggered a sequential detail-page visit just to obtain an exact publication timestamp,\n- target ordering favored current RUNNING bot segments, so stale/unfinished models such as tablet/iPad rows could wait behind a large Samsung queue.\n\n## Fix\n\n### 1. Fast incremental publication path\nHealthy incremental scans no longer open one Vinted detail page per newly discovered listing.\n\nFor a post-baseline incremental discovery:\n- the scan remains complete without a detail-page timestamp lookup,\n- backend persists firstSeenAt as the publication-time fallback,\n- exact detail-page resolution is still mandatory for baseline recovery, incomplete publication windows, known rows missing a timestamp, and explicit full-catalog recovery.\n\nThis keeps historical recovery strict while making normal recurring scans much faster.\n\n### 2. Fill unfinished/stale models first\nBackend target ordering now prioritizes:\n1. missing/incomplete baseline/publication coverage,\n2. oldest last successful scan,\n3. existing RUNNING-bot business priority,\n4. stable brand/model ordering.\n\nSo rows that still show incomplete Observer coverage no longer sit behind every active Samsung model.\n\n### 3. Freeze target order for a whole pass\nBecause scan-state freshness changes while a pass is running, Playwright now freezes the model order from the first batch and reuses it across browser recycling and retries. This prevents dynamic stale-first ordering from causing duplicate/skipped targets.\n\n### 4. Reduce browser restart overhead\nDefault Observer browser recycle size increases from 3 to 6 model targets. It is still bounded/configurable and the same single headed/headless Observer browser is recycled; this does not increase Observer concurrency.\n\n## Safety\n- no changes to negotiation decisions, real-offer actions, quota/idempotency, or session persistence\n- full/baseline historical reconstruction still requires exact Vinted publication timestamps\n- healthy incremental fallback only applies to newly discovered post-baseline rows\n- target order remains frozen during an in-progress pass so resume indexes remain correct",
